1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,540
Koji Satake. I'm looking forward to our game today.

2
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:12,240
I'm Nozomi Date. Glad to finally meet you. Good luck.

3
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:17,540
You know, you are the type of midfielder I love to watch during a game.

4
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:21,360
So focused. Always the calm, intelligent playmaker.

5
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,920
I get a little embarrassed when someone brings up my playing days.

6
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,780
Were you in J League too?

7
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:29,780
If you count the handful of games in J3 I played.

8
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:33,180
Well, regardless, you built a wonderful team here.

9
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:39,140
It's wild to think that these were the lesser-known players at one time. You've really done some great work.

10
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,940
Helps that I relate to them. I know what it's like to never be seen as the star player. Too well.

11
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:51,940
Tachivana!

12
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:54,220
Hey, guys!

13
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:59,420
I can't believe you never came to visit us. You're playing, right?

14
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:01,520
Yeah, and looking forward to it.

15
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:04,520
It's great to see you after all this time. You're looking good.

16
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:09,140
Anyway, is everything okay with your teammates out there?

17
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:16,160
I've never seen anyone look so freaked out and panicked just while warming up.

18
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:17,340
That's it.

19
00:01:17,340 --> 00:01:38,700
That's it. Warm-up's over. Both teams should return to your locker rooms immediately.

20
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:47,740
hey you guys go on in i'm gonna hang out with her for a few

21
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:55,860
what the heck is takashima doing seriously yep that really just happened

22
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:59,700
but why now he doesn't have very long

23
00:03:31,642 --> 00:03:34,602
What's going on? Why is everyone so tense?

24
00:03:34,802 --> 00:03:37,362
I don't remember the last time I saw you all so nervous.

25
00:03:38,022 --> 00:03:42,962
Well, anyways, be sure to use the countermeasures we've been working on this past week from the very start.

26
00:03:43,422 --> 00:03:46,642
It would be a shame if you were all too tense to benefit from your hard work.

27
00:03:47,362 --> 00:03:51,022
Individually, you guys are better than them. Don't forget that out there.

28
00:03:51,102 --> 00:03:53,722
Please don't say that. It's bad luck to hear before a game.

29
00:03:54,002 --> 00:03:56,542
Yeah, you basically just pep-talked us into losing.

30
00:03:56,722 --> 00:04:00,982
It's because we're better individually that we are terrified of losing to them as a team.

31
00:04:01,002 --> 00:04:02,762
I don't know what will happen to us after!

32
00:04:06,582 --> 00:04:10,662
As usual, you're all useless and incompetent.

33
00:04:12,662 --> 00:04:15,342
Hey, listen up. I have some advice for-

34
00:04:15,342 --> 00:04:20,982
Hey, I'm back. Sorry it took so long.

35
00:04:25,362 --> 00:04:26,342
I'm good now.

36
00:04:26,442 --> 00:04:29,002
Thanks, Ty. I can tell you're a barber's daughter.

37
00:04:29,002 --> 00:04:33,642
So, Takashima, is there a story behind your new look?

38
00:04:34,582 --> 00:04:37,962
Nah, just tradition. It's what you do if you have a red pompadour.

39
00:04:38,082 --> 00:04:40,262
Apparently, shaving it off helps to psych you up.

40
00:04:40,662 --> 00:04:41,562
How do I look?

41
00:04:41,562 --> 00:04:51,942
Wait, for real? You shaved off your hair right before a game? No way!

42
00:04:53,682 --> 00:04:56,282
I had to do something about your pathetic faces.

43
00:04:57,002 --> 00:04:58,682
This isn't an easy game for us.

44
00:04:59,182 --> 00:05:00,682
We need to go out psyched.

45
00:05:00,682 --> 00:05:04,622
Takashima's right, you guys.

46
00:05:04,942 --> 00:05:07,302
The fact is, we've done everything we can.

47
00:05:07,822 --> 00:05:10,002
We're way below Musashino in the league.

48
00:05:10,522 --> 00:05:11,982
That makes us underdogs.

49
00:05:12,222 --> 00:05:14,102
But that doesn't mean we can't win today!

50
00:05:14,322 --> 00:05:15,322
And we're going to!

51
00:05:15,582 --> 00:05:17,422
Yeah! Let's do it, guys!

52
00:05:17,542 --> 00:05:18,882
He's right! Bring it on!

53
00:05:18,882 --> 00:05:23,902
Togashima, remember what you said when you were on the junior team?

54
00:05:24,762 --> 00:05:26,382
You were right all along, you know?

55
00:05:27,262 --> 00:05:29,302
Winning should always be the priority.

56
00:05:30,562 --> 00:05:31,582
Think about it.

57
00:05:31,822 --> 00:05:34,382
If we don't win, then neither of you get to be right.

58
00:05:36,262 --> 00:05:37,462
And it doesn't matter.

59
00:05:37,822 --> 00:05:38,722
So let's win.

60
00:05:38,722 --> 00:05:54,742
It's finally here.

61
00:05:55,402 --> 00:05:57,582
The moment I've been waiting for.

62
00:06:08,722 --> 00:06:12,802
We want the Musashino countermeasure in full gear from kickoff.

63
00:06:12,982 --> 00:06:13,582
You got that?

64
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:15,662
Take a good look at them over there.

65
00:06:16,682 --> 00:06:18,822
We know every single one of them.

66
00:06:19,142 --> 00:06:22,622
And we've been showing them how much better we are than them since we were children.

67
00:06:23,422 --> 00:06:26,542
Play the same game we always have and we can't lose!

68
00:06:26,822 --> 00:06:27,302
Yeah!

69
00:06:33,382 --> 00:06:35,122
There it is! The high press!

70
00:06:38,722 --> 00:06:46,702
Hurry up! This way!

71
00:06:50,642 --> 00:06:52,502
He rushed them just to play it backwards?

72
00:06:53,002 --> 00:06:54,222
Put some pressure on him!

73
00:06:58,182 --> 00:07:00,242
They're amazing. All of them.

74
00:07:00,722 --> 00:07:01,702
I know, right?

75
00:07:01,702 --> 00:07:03,462
Their strategy is predictable, though.

76
00:07:03,722 --> 00:07:05,022
They're just hitting long balls.

77
00:07:05,462 --> 00:07:06,562
Are they doing that on purpose?

78
00:07:06,562 --> 00:07:10,322
Owie! Over to you!

79
00:07:10,942 --> 00:07:11,522
It's true.

80
00:07:12,082 --> 00:07:13,942
We thrive on our individual skills.

81
00:07:14,562 --> 00:07:15,562
It's our advantage.

82
00:07:16,522 --> 00:07:17,982
And if we lean on it more,

83
00:07:18,462 --> 00:07:20,062
a simple tactic could work wonders.

84
00:07:20,382 --> 00:07:21,842
Even against the high press,

85
00:07:22,022 --> 00:07:23,542
we could take them by surprise.

86
00:07:24,602 --> 00:07:25,682
What that means is,

87
00:07:25,762 --> 00:07:26,922
if you want a shot at this,

88
00:07:27,202 --> 00:07:29,122
brush up on your long ball technique.

89
00:07:29,122 --> 00:07:31,622
Let me tell you something.

90
00:07:32,542 --> 00:07:34,242
I don't have a lot of skills.

91
00:07:34,742 --> 00:07:35,362
At all!

92
00:07:35,882 --> 00:07:38,542
No matter how many times I stayed behind to practice,

93
00:07:38,782 --> 00:07:40,022
I still sucked!

94
00:07:40,342 --> 00:07:41,102
But you know what?

95
00:07:41,542 --> 00:07:43,182
It'll help if you verbalize everything,

96
00:07:43,262 --> 00:07:44,422
one long pass at a time.

97
00:07:44,962 --> 00:07:46,362
And be sure to make eye contact.

98
00:07:47,042 --> 00:07:48,922
Communicate with your eyes before you pass.

99
00:07:49,082 --> 00:07:49,842
Every time.

100
00:07:49,842 --> 00:07:57,822
They helped me practice,

101
00:07:58,222 --> 00:07:59,622
and never gave up on me.

102
00:08:00,482 --> 00:08:02,922
This long pass is for each of them.

103
00:08:03,422 --> 00:08:05,222
And it's gonna make it all the way through.

104
00:08:06,222 --> 00:08:08,342
Just approach the ball diagonally.

105
00:08:09,102 --> 00:08:10,522
The toes of your planted foot

106
00:08:10,522 --> 00:08:12,222
should always point where you want the ball.

107
00:08:12,962 --> 00:08:14,742
Extend your toes and lock your ankle.

108
00:08:14,742 --> 00:08:17,042
and then come down

109
00:08:17,042 --> 00:08:18,362
and hit the middle of the ball

110
00:08:18,362 --> 00:08:19,642
with the top of your foot.

111
00:08:22,642 --> 00:08:24,102
The long ball got through!

112
00:08:24,722 --> 00:08:26,062
He's clear the whole way!

113
00:08:32,982 --> 00:08:33,802
For real?

114
00:08:34,262 --> 00:08:34,982
Damn it!

115
00:08:44,742 --> 00:08:54,542
Well, it looks like Asperion's tactic today

116
00:08:54,542 --> 00:08:55,622
is trying to go direct.

117
00:08:55,962 --> 00:08:56,822
They've chosen a style

118
00:08:56,822 --> 00:08:59,002
that isn't so focused on retaining ball possession.

119
00:08:59,482 --> 00:09:01,242
Going direct is a good call for them.

120
00:09:01,762 --> 00:09:04,102
It's a proven formula against the high press.

121
00:09:04,482 --> 00:09:05,982
All of Musashino's players

122
00:09:05,982 --> 00:09:07,582
contribute to the high press.

123
00:09:07,962 --> 00:09:08,702
So naturally,

124
00:09:08,702 --> 00:09:10,662
that will help create numerous spaces

125
00:09:10,662 --> 00:09:11,782
in their part of the field.

126
00:09:12,662 --> 00:09:13,782
Then they'll be vulnerable.

127
00:09:13,782 --> 00:09:15,962
With plenty of room for long balls

128
00:09:15,962 --> 00:09:17,442
if all goes as planned.

129
00:09:17,962 --> 00:09:18,822
Oh, it's gotta.

130
00:09:19,602 --> 00:09:21,842
Coach Nozomi had them practicing long balls

131
00:09:21,842 --> 00:09:22,982
for a whole week straight.

132
00:09:23,882 --> 00:09:25,342
And like you pointed out,

133
00:09:25,622 --> 00:09:27,002
they're like one-trick ponies.

134
00:09:27,602 --> 00:09:29,042
I'm willing to bet a lot of teams

135
00:09:29,042 --> 00:09:30,042
that face Musashino

136
00:09:30,042 --> 00:09:31,342
will go with the same tactic.

137
00:09:32,362 --> 00:09:32,822
However,

138
00:09:33,222 --> 00:09:35,522
what sets Asperion apart from other teams is

139
00:09:35,522 --> 00:09:36,442
their skill.

140
00:09:38,122 --> 00:09:38,982
Hey, Ultimo!

141
00:09:39,282 --> 00:09:40,262
Quit forcing it!

142
00:09:40,482 --> 00:09:41,302
Pass it back!

143
00:09:41,302 --> 00:09:46,922
Staying after training

144
00:09:46,922 --> 00:09:48,122
wasn't such a bad idea.

145
00:09:49,122 --> 00:09:51,182
I actually learned by teaching.

146
00:09:51,562 --> 00:09:52,902
Like I was talking it through

147
00:09:52,902 --> 00:09:54,282
and explaining it to myself.

148
00:09:54,642 --> 00:09:56,442
It was also great to hear their ideas.

149
00:09:57,102 --> 00:09:58,742
Spending time with them in that way

150
00:09:58,742 --> 00:10:00,442
made all the difference.

151
00:10:00,442 --> 00:10:06,742
Come on!

152
00:10:07,122 --> 00:10:08,482
How'd I miss that?

153
00:10:08,502 --> 00:10:09,662
Don't worry about it!

154
00:10:09,822 --> 00:10:10,822
You'll get the next one!

155
00:10:12,102 --> 00:10:12,942
It's working!

156
00:10:13,622 --> 00:10:15,262
Musashino's high press can't function!

157
00:10:15,622 --> 00:10:17,122
We've still got a chance to win!

158
00:10:17,862 --> 00:10:19,602
They're not using this tactic as a group.

159
00:10:19,862 --> 00:10:21,442
It's just all about making the most

160
00:10:21,442 --> 00:10:23,042
of their individual strengths, right?

161
00:10:23,042 --> 00:10:23,662
Yep!

162
00:10:24,222 --> 00:10:25,642
Well, for the moment at least.

163
00:10:26,302 --> 00:10:27,182
And that's it?

164
00:10:27,522 --> 00:10:28,042
Huh?

165
00:10:28,662 --> 00:10:30,922
One trick is all they've got.

166
00:10:30,922 --> 00:10:40,282
Going with long balls, huh?

167
00:10:40,862 --> 00:10:42,182
I honestly didn't expect

168
00:10:42,182 --> 00:10:43,422
Esperion to fall back

169
00:10:43,422 --> 00:10:44,662
on such a beginner tactic.

170
00:10:45,302 --> 00:10:47,462
But you guys have some strong players

171
00:10:47,462 --> 00:10:48,242
and you seem to have

172
00:10:48,242 --> 00:10:49,302
a good flow on the field.

173
00:10:49,622 --> 00:10:50,442
Well, sorta.

174
00:10:50,482 --> 00:10:51,242
What's that mean?

175
00:10:51,242 --> 00:10:54,302
I need you to deliver a message for me

176
00:10:54,302 --> 00:10:56,682
to that loser player you have.

177
00:10:57,622 --> 00:10:58,682
For it to work,

178
00:10:58,762 --> 00:11:00,262
he needed to score back there.

179
00:11:00,722 --> 00:11:02,582
But he couldn't seal the deal.

180
00:11:03,282 --> 00:11:04,102
After the game,

181
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:06,642
he'll realize that was the fatal blow.

182
00:11:07,022 --> 00:11:08,482
The one that ended it all.

183
00:11:21,242 --> 00:11:34,462
Yeah!

184
00:11:35,122 --> 00:11:36,642
Here comes the second attempt!

185
00:11:37,602 --> 00:11:38,742
But first,

186
00:11:38,962 --> 00:11:40,322
I gotta make eye contact.

187
00:11:42,722 --> 00:11:44,462
Hit the middle of the ball.

188
00:11:45,002 --> 00:11:45,902
The middle of the ball!

189
00:11:46,542 --> 00:11:47,742
I can do this!

190
00:11:48,682 --> 00:11:49,442
Boom!

191
00:11:51,242 --> 00:11:52,282
There it is!

192
00:11:52,642 --> 00:11:55,162
Nice. That's excellent space, Aoi. Way to go.

193
00:11:59,362 --> 00:12:00,902
What? No way!

194
00:12:06,242 --> 00:12:07,662
Damn, he stole it!

195
00:12:08,282 --> 00:12:08,922
Hold it!

196
00:12:19,362 --> 00:12:20,762
Togashi's amazing.

197
00:12:21,242 --> 00:12:24,362
His kicks are powerful, but he keeps them smooth and controlled.

198
00:12:27,962 --> 00:12:28,762
Nakano!

199
00:12:47,722 --> 00:12:50,002
Man! That was so close!

200
00:12:50,002 --> 00:12:51,122
If I hadn't brought him down...

201
00:12:51,122 --> 00:12:56,242
Kahnata could have totally scored, just like he did then!

202
00:12:56,242 --> 00:13:01,362
Sweet! Perfect place for a free kick!

203
00:13:01,362 --> 00:13:04,482
They got a yellow card in the first 15 minutes?

204
00:13:04,482 --> 00:13:06,482
How is that even possible?

205
00:13:06,482 --> 00:13:07,602
Damn it!

206
00:13:07,602 --> 00:13:09,602
Damn it! I'm so sorry!

207
00:13:09,602 --> 00:13:11,602
Nah, man, don't sweat it! You were just trying to defend the best you could!

208
00:13:11,602 --> 00:13:16,722
Hey, move more into the middle!

209
00:13:16,722 --> 00:13:17,842
A yellow card!

210
00:13:17,842 --> 00:13:19,842
I guess I need to be more careful!

211
00:13:19,842 --> 00:13:22,962
I guess I need to be more careful!

212
00:13:22,962 --> 00:13:24,082
I guess I need to be more careful!

213
00:13:24,082 --> 00:13:26,082
But what was that?

214
00:13:26,082 --> 00:13:27,202
Those two long balls earlier!

215
00:13:27,202 --> 00:13:31,202
Five minutes ago, they would have gone through just fine!

216
00:13:31,202 --> 00:13:34,322
Five minutes ago, they would have gone through just fine!

217
00:13:34,322 --> 00:13:36,322
Five minutes ago, they would have gone through just fine!

218
00:13:36,322 --> 00:13:38,322
Why not now? What happened?

219
00:13:38,322 --> 00:13:39,442
Interesting!

220
00:13:39,442 --> 00:13:42,802
They're leaving Tachibana and their number 12 up front!

221
00:13:43,602 --> 00:13:46,242
They're gonna keep trying to counter it with a long ball!

222
00:13:46,882 --> 00:13:47,922
So be on the lookout!

223
00:13:48,802 --> 00:13:51,842
I don't know how long they've been planning it, but at least we know now!

224
00:13:56,882 --> 00:14:00,242
Kaneda! Trust me! Do what I said!

225
00:14:02,642 --> 00:14:05,202
I feel sick! Something's not right!

226
00:14:06,002 --> 00:14:10,242
Those two! He and Kaneda were going at each other!

227
00:14:11,762 --> 00:14:13,602
So what were they talking about?

228
00:14:14,402 --> 00:14:17,442
Guys! Listen up! Use the direct approach all the way!

229
00:14:18,002 --> 00:14:19,682
They can't counter our tactics!

230
00:14:20,402 --> 00:14:22,642
Lean on your technique to punch through!

231
00:14:22,642 --> 00:14:24,322
What? Going direct won't cut it!

232
00:14:25,042 --> 00:14:26,322
It's not like that anymore!

233
00:14:26,962 --> 00:14:27,522
Kodada?

234
00:14:28,722 --> 00:14:31,362
Musashino's adjusted their tactics in the last few minutes!

235
00:14:32,482 --> 00:14:34,642
That's their response to our direct approach!

236
00:14:34,642 --> 00:14:36,562
They're gonna wait for us to step further back!

237
00:14:37,362 --> 00:14:40,722
That means their reaction time will be intentionally shorter once the ball is kicked!

238
00:14:41,522 --> 00:14:42,882
They've got us all figured out!

239
00:14:43,602 --> 00:14:44,802
Five, six...

240
00:14:44,802 --> 00:14:48,322
I don't get it! How did they adjust to make a new plan so quickly?

241
00:14:48,322 --> 00:14:49,922
That guy! Number 10!

242
00:14:52,162 --> 00:14:53,122
Chiaki Muto!

243
00:14:54,162 --> 00:14:55,762
He's an incredible playmaker!

244
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:59,042
He... he's the playmaker?

245
00:14:59,042 --> 00:15:12,162
Huh?

246
00:15:14,162 --> 00:15:16,562
There's space out in front! Block it off!

247
00:15:16,562 --> 00:15:27,122
He's in no rush. Instead of attacking, he calms the team down by playing back passes.

248
00:15:27,122 --> 00:15:37,762
That was also his plan earlier, when they got the free kick in front of the goal. It was a huge opportunity to score. But Muto just went around talking to his teammates.

249
00:15:37,762 --> 00:15:51,042
He was probably already telling them about the new game plan. His demeanor affects them. He makes the whole team calm. He's an excellent captain. And a brilliant playmaker!

250
00:15:51,762 --> 00:15:57,762
We're only 17 minutes into the match. They're adjusting to our strategy too quickly. Damn it!

251
00:15:57,762 --> 00:16:06,962
They're already starting to hesitate. Not good. They're in trouble.

252
00:16:06,962 --> 00:16:09,842
Aspirion's got no one to calm them down.

253
00:16:11,842 --> 00:16:19,922
What in the world is going on? Why is everyone's mood such trash? Did you all forget what we've been working on this entire week?

254
00:16:20,962 --> 00:16:25,842
Come on, guys! Don't start doubting yourselves! We are going to win this!

255
00:16:25,842 --> 00:16:41,762
You don't need to go out of your way to get the ball. We know they're going to screw up. That'll be your chance to shine.

256
00:16:45,282 --> 00:16:50,642
Whoa! A short pass now, huh? Okay, I guess we'll just reset here and then...

257
00:16:50,642 --> 00:16:54,882
I didn't kick hard enough!

258
00:17:00,642 --> 00:17:02,562
That's what you think. Not on mine!

259
00:17:08,722 --> 00:17:09,522
That was close.

260
00:17:20,642 --> 00:17:32,082
Man! Screw this guy!

261
00:17:33,282 --> 00:17:37,122
You can't just leave that monster unmarked. Not this time.

262
00:17:38,962 --> 00:17:40,802
He knows where the ball's going.

263
00:17:41,682 --> 00:17:44,562
That reaction to a passing error was insane.

264
00:17:44,562 --> 00:17:48,562
His mid-range shots are crazy accurate. Dude can shoot from anywhere.

265
00:17:48,562 --> 00:17:55,922
Just once. We mess up once and he gets to score. And it's bound to happen. As long as he's still around.

266
00:17:57,842 --> 00:18:01,842
High press, without hesitation. Everyone working as a single unit.

267
00:18:02,802 --> 00:18:06,722
One playmaker to coordinate them. And one pure striker.

268
00:18:07,442 --> 00:18:11,842
We have everything Aspirion doesn't. Almost feels like an unfair advantage.

269
00:18:11,842 --> 00:18:19,202
I think we should bring back man-marking. Because that guy can't be trusted.

270
00:18:19,202 --> 00:18:28,482
Of course he's getting aggressive. Now that our long balls aren't working. Before anything else, we seriously need to rethink our marking.

271
00:18:28,482 --> 00:18:33,922
Hey guys! Listen! I want to take over marking Kaneda.

272
00:18:36,402 --> 00:18:40,882
Positionally, I'm his matchup. So I'll mark him. It makes the most sense.

273
00:18:40,882 --> 00:18:47,282
You only switched to playing defense recently. Do you even know how to man-mark properly? Be honest.

274
00:18:47,282 --> 00:18:49,602
What the heck, man? Why are you fighting me on this?

275
00:18:49,602 --> 00:18:51,362
Just let me do it. Huh?

276
00:18:53,122 --> 00:18:55,522
Trust me. I need to do this.

277
00:18:57,842 --> 00:19:02,962
Kaneda has sure grown a lot, hasn't he? Amazing. Remember tryouts last year?

278
00:19:03,442 --> 00:19:08,402
That aggression was all that made him stand out. But his technique and speed have improved.

279
00:19:09,122 --> 00:19:13,602
His build is quite impressive. All that progress has increased his confidence.

280
00:19:13,602 --> 00:19:19,682
That's important for our defense. But no need to worry. When it's about playing soccer,

281
00:19:19,682 --> 00:19:23,602
our players have all the skills to back it up. I know they do.

282
00:19:23,602 --> 00:19:27,282
Uh-huh. Long ball incoming! Be careful!

283
00:19:30,162 --> 00:19:38,082
What? They've adjusted their play. Stopped relying on long balls. Now they're playing more short passes.

284
00:19:38,082 --> 00:19:44,322
We have to remember that possession soccer is a spirion specialty. What's the best way to handle this?

285
00:19:49,282 --> 00:19:51,122
Saki! Incoming! Got it!

286
00:19:53,842 --> 00:19:55,522
Nakano! Hit Takaneda!

287
00:19:58,082 --> 00:19:59,122
Yes!

288
00:19:59,122 --> 00:20:12,402
Are they for real? That little guy is marking him? I don't think this is going to end very well.

289
00:20:13,042 --> 00:20:16,802
Positioning is the most important thing in man-to-man marking. No question there.

290
00:20:18,802 --> 00:20:23,602
Always keep a good distance from your opponent. You have to be able to observe his movement,

291
00:20:23,602 --> 00:20:29,042
so you can predict what he'll do next. And then... Take it! Come on!

292
00:20:33,602 --> 00:20:37,362
Physique differences don't matter. When it comes to the basic skills,

293
00:20:38,002 --> 00:20:43,762
a spirion is the best. It looks like other players are adjusting now too, using short passes.

294
00:20:44,482 --> 00:20:48,722
They just have to play their game. If they do, there's no way we're gonna lose today.

295
00:20:48,722 --> 00:20:50,962
It's Tsukishima. Huh?

296
00:20:52,482 --> 00:20:55,442
A real-life game doesn't play out the way you think it will on paper.

297
00:20:57,282 --> 00:20:59,842
All right! Now to Kickstarter possession, sucker!

298
00:21:11,682 --> 00:21:16,562
He's seriously fast! Huh? Whoa! And so is the little guy who's marking him!

299
00:21:18,722 --> 00:21:23,682
KANIDAAA!

300
00:21:28,722 --> 00:21:30,402
There you go! Pin him in there!

301
00:21:32,082 --> 00:21:37,682
Quit making it so hard! This is supposed to be a game, a sport! I shouldn't have to deal with this

302
00:21:37,682 --> 00:21:40,162
kind of hostility! Now move!

303
00:21:45,282 --> 00:21:45,602
Nice!

304
00:21:48,722 --> 00:21:59,362
The angle's too tight! There's no way!

305
00:21:59,362 --> 00:22:01,762
Hey!

306
00:22:02,482 --> 00:22:07,362
You pieces of shit!

307
00:22:07,522 --> 00:22:09,842
HA!

308
00:22:10,002 --> 00:22:12,082
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

309
00:22:12,082 --> 00:22:12,962
Ugh!

310
00:22:16,962 --> 00:22:18,002
taught меня!

311
00:22:18,082 --> 00:22:19,042
KANIDA!

312
00:22:19,042 --> 00:22:21,082
ut

313
00:22:22,162 --> 00:22:23,122
us

314
00:22:24,322 --> 00:22:24,882
got

315
00:22:24,882 --> 00:22:26,402
Aaron

316
00:22:26,402 --> 00:22:26,722
us

317
00:22:26,722 --> 00:22:27,922
an

318
00:22:27,922 --> 00:22:28,002
us

319
00:22:28,002 --> 00:22:29,002
us

320
00:22:29,002 --> 00:22:58,982
We'll be right back.

321
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:27,406
Next time on Owlash, like a demon.

